    "verdict": "MIXED, reported precisely rather than rounded to a single word: (1) the 93-99pct atom-level lost-interaction dominance was PARTIALLY -- not wholly -- a representation artifact: correcting to residue-level granularity (the established SIFt/ProLIF convention) reduces it to ~85pct, consistently across both independent sample sizes (24 and 50 compounds), a real and reproducible effect. (2) The core alpha-favored-motif finding does NOT change qualitatively: at the corrected granularity, alpha-selective compounds still fail to show the predicted enrichment (net alpha-vs-other-favored score for alpha_selective is -0.83 in both datasets, WORSE than or tied with other_selective in both). The negative result therefore survives chemically meaningful aggregation and is not primarily a granularity artifact -- this is now stronger evidence against the simple, single-residue alpha-favored-motif hypothesis than the original atom-level finding alone provided.",
